# Who reviews a change here. The branch protection rule on `main` requires an
# approval from someone named below, and GitHub never counts a pull request's
# own author toward it, so every change is read by a second maintainer.
#
# One rule for the whole tree: these maintainers review across it rather than
# owning separate areas, and a per-path split would have to name owners this
# project does not have yet. Split it the day an area gets a distinct owner --
# a later, more specific rule wins over this one.
#
# Every name here needs write access to the repository; a name that does not
# have it is silently ignored, which reads exactly like a working rule.
